{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo Show 8 gives me a reason to consider another Alexa device: its larger screen could add something useful alongside my recent Show 5.",
    "The 16TB external drive fits my earlier backup drive and recovery-plan purchases by offering more storage capacity. The USB adapters also appeal as a way to keep using existing accessories, provided I have a compatible USB-C device."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The streaming sticks and older Dot and Show 5 repeat functions covered by my recently purchased 4K Max, fourth-generation Dot, and second-generation Show 5.",
    "Using Alexa at home does not mean I need it in my car, and buying Bluetooth mice and keyboards does not mean I am currently looking for wireless earbuds."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Alexa purchases seem to have been treated as interest in almost any Alexa device, regardless of whether it adds a useful capability.",
    "My interest in connected computer accessories seems to have been stretched into interest in personal audio, although those purchases serve different needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases matter because they show which needs I have already covered; older versions of those devices give me little reason to buy again.",
    "I have a reason to consider additions that expand what I can do, such as a larger display or more backup storage. For adapters, compatibility with devices I actually own is essential."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my home electronics interests but miss the difference between a useful addition and another device that repeats what I already have."
}"}
